# Build context exclusions for `docker build`. Anything listed here is
# NOT shipped into image layers, even if `COPY . .` appears in a Dockerfile.
#
# Round 3 / PR-A — secrets sweep.
# Root cause of A01-P0-001: the prior allowlist only covered `.env.local`
# and `.env.production`, leaving `.env`, `.env.backup`, and
# `tests/**/.env.test` to be baked into images via `COPY . .`. The block
# below excludes every env-bearing path and explicitly re-allows only
# placeholder/template files.

# ⚠️ `**/` IS LOAD-BEARING ON THESE TWO. A BARE DIRECTORY NAME MATCHES ONLY AT
# THE CONTEXT ROOT — `node_modules` does NOT exclude `apps/transcribe-md/
# node_modules`, and `.next` does NOT exclude `apps/*/.next`. Both were being
# shipped into the build context and copied over the installed ones by
# `COPY . .`.
#
# PROVED, 2026-08-14: a build from a git WORKTREE failed with
#   `cannot replace to directory /app/apps/transcribe-md/node_modules with file`
# because the nested path is a SYMLINK there and Docker cannot replace a
# directory with a file. In `/opt/meddoc-pro` the same paths are real
# directories, so the identical mistake fails SILENTLY instead of loudly — the
# build "works" while overlaying host modules onto the image's.
#
# ⚠️ AND LINE `apps/*/.next/standalone/**/.env` BELOW IS THIS BUG'S OWN
# FOOTPRINT: somebody hit the `.next` gap, and patched the symptom (one env path
# inside it) rather than the pattern. It is deliberately LEFT in place —
# defence in depth on a secrets block is not something to trim while fixing
# build hygiene.
#
# The other four need no `**/`, checked rather than assumed: the only nested
# `docs` and `.claude` live under `landing-monolith/`, and the only nested
# `.git` under `.local/` — both already excluded outright below.
**/node_modules
**/.next
.git
.claude
backups
docs

# Env-family — exclude EVERYTHING by default, allow only documented placeholders.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.env.local
*.env.backup
tests/**/.env.test
apps/*/.env
apps/*/.env.local
apps/*/.env.backup
apps/*/.next/standalone/**/.env
!.env.example
!.env.test.example
!.env.production.example
!.env.phase-6.2.template

# Secret-bearing build artefacts that have leaked before.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.aws/
.gnupg/
**/*.bak

# Other build-context noise that should never ship.
*.md
test-results
playwright-report
coverage
.vitest-cache
.turbo
.cache
tmp
out

# ── Build-context weight (full-app audit 2026-07-24) ────────────────────────
# `COPY . .` in apps/*/Dockerfile ships the ENTIRE repo root into the builder
# layer. Only `apps/*` and `packages/*` are npm workspaces, so everything below
# is dead weight that made a cold build spend minutes on a single COPY.
#
# NOTE on secrets/: it holds a 1 GB LUKS container (pgdata.luks). It never
# reached the FINAL image — the runner stage copies only the standalone build,
# so multi-stage kept it out (verified against the running prod container) —
# but it was being shipped into the build CONTEXT and the builder layer, which
# is both slow and the wrong place for a volume image to live.
.local

# ── GIT WORKTREES AT THE CONTEXT ROOT ───────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ MEASURED 2026-09-05: the build context was 4.04 GB for `db-migrate` and
# 4.02 GB for the app — about 8 GB and 84 seconds shipped to the daemon on
# EVERY deploy. 24 git worktrees live beside the repo at ~155 MB of source
# each. Their `node_modules` were already excluded above, which is exactly
# what left each one small enough that nobody noticed it — and there are
# twenty-four.
#
# WHY IT WENT UNNOTICED. The worktree discipline is deliberate and recent: the
# shared tree is a deploy surface, so all feature work moved into worktrees
# BESIDE it. That rule was about GIT SAFETY, and nobody re-asked what it did
# to the BUILD. A directory invisible to `git status` is not invisible to
# `docker build`.
#
# SAFE BY CONSTRUCTION, CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED: no `COPY` in any
# Dockerfile names a dot-path at the context root — the named copies are
# package.json files, `apps/` and `packages/` — so nothing here is reachable
# except through `COPY . .`, which wants none of it.
#
# ⚠️ THIS LIST WILL GO STALE, BECAUSE WORKTREE NAMES ARE AD HOC. That is what
# `scripts/check-dockerignore-covers-worktrees.sh` exists for: it reads
# `git worktree list` and fails, naming any root worktree this file does not
# cover. A static list without that check is a fix with a decay date.
.wt-*
.r16*
.p17*
.p18*
.pass-*
.cdev
.f*-build
.f8-s2-recon
secrets
landing-monolith
venv
_design-references
audit-evidence
audit-final-evidence

# Loose capture artefacts that accumulate at the repo ROOT (157 of them at the
# time of writing). Anchored with a leading slash ON PURPOSE: a bare `*.png`
# would also exclude apps/*/public/**, so the day someone adds a real image
# asset the build would silently ship without it. There are no image assets in
# any app's public/ today — this rule keeps it that way by construction rather
# than by luck.
/*.jpeg
/*.jpg
/*.png
/*.zip
/*.pdf
/*.docx
